    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0706" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv12/pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 181.9202/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Bandholtz to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-26">August 26, 1919</date>.<lb/>[Received August 27—11
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>29. From two sources have received information that Roumania’s attitude is due
                    Prime Minister, who is striving to ensure victory his party in fall elections by
                    display rich spoils of war from Hungary. To prevent anarchy in case of
                    precipitate Roumanian evacuation of all Hungary, it is of prime importance that
                    the Roumanians permit the immediate reorganization and arming of the municipal
                    police, that they release interned Hungarian officers and that they stay east of
                    the Danube. No government has yet been formed, but this Mission is daily
                    besieged by delegations demanding suitable representation in <pb facs="0707"
                        n="657" xml:id="pg657"/> the ministry, to all of whom is given the
                    stereotyped reply that we cannot mix in the internal affairs of Hungary.</p>
                <p>The anti-Semitic question is getting rather serious; reports were received
                    yesterday that many Jews had been beaten in the streets of the city. Most of the
                    petitions received insist that there be no Jews in the government.</p>
                <p>Telegram No. 10<anchor n="24" xml:id="d281-f1"/> received and copies furnished my
                    colleagues.</p>
                <p>Receipt acknowledged of No. 8.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d281-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bandholtz</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
